Use items to get keys and values together:
```python
marks = {'math': 90, 'art': 80}
for subject, score in marks.items():
    print(subject, score)
```

items use karo, isse key aur value dono ek saath milte hain:
```python
marks = {'math': 90, 'art': 80}
for subject, score in marks.items():
    print(subject, score)
```

items इस्तेमाल कीजिए, इससे कुंजी और मान दोनों साथ मिलते हैं:
```python
marks = {'math': 90, 'art': 80}
for subject, score in marks.items():
    print(subject, score)
```

A function can call itself:
```python
def fact(n):
    if n <= 1:
        return 1
    return n * fact(n - 1)
print(fact(5))
```
This prints 120.

Function khud ko call kar sakta hai:
```python
def fact(n):
    if n <= 1:
        return 1
    return n * fact(n - 1)
print(fact(5))
```
Ye 120 print karta hai.

फ़ंक्शन खुद को बुला सकता है:
```python
def fact(n):
    if n <= 1:
        return 1
    return n * fact(n - 1)
print(fact(5))
```
यह 120 प्रिंट करता है।

class keyword use karo:
```python
class Dog:
    def bark(self):
        print('Woof')
Dog().bark()
```
Ye Woof print karta hai.

class कीवर्ड इस्तेमाल कीजिए:
```python
class Dog:
    def bark(self):
        print('Woof')
Dog().bark()
```
यह Woof प्रिंट करता है।

